A||||5||FieroMike||Blown Rod
Z||000000||FieroMike||05-20-99||10:20 AM||||I need a little advice please!!!  Yesterday I went to about 4500 rpm and then let the engine wind down to slow me down and it REALLY started slowing down so I put the clutch in and the engine died.  It started back up but knocked really bad about 2000 RPM.  I checked it out and it's a blown rod!! That sucks.  My question is I am getting a rebuild and I need to take out the engine.  Which is easier?  Out the top or out the bottom?  Any suggestions would be appreciated. Thanks!<br>Mike
Z||000001||theogre||05-20-99||11:42 AM||||seems to me, that out the top w/ a 4cyl should be least painfull for most people. There's plenty of room..... I'd cut a peice of scrap wood to protect the window in case something shifts.<p>You can get the cradle out fairly easy if you have a lift. people have done it without a lift, it's allot of jacking and blocking, and god help you if something moves.
Z||000002||FieroMike||05-20-99||03:41 PM||||Ogre,<br>I have a 2.8 V-6.  Any idea on the time frames of either one?  I will do which ever one is faster probably.  I need to drive to work! :-)<br>Thanks
Z||000003||Carrolles||05-20-99||03:47 PM||||Remember to place a board or something against the rear glass when you remove the deck lid to protect it from accidentally getting smashed by the lid spring.
Z||000004||theogre||05-20-99||07:34 PM||||I expect with a 6 out the bottom might be a bit faster.... but not by much.
Z||000005||FieroMike||05-21-99||02:08 PM||||Thanks!!!  It's coming out the bottom then.  One good this is that this give me a chance to have the engine rebuilt, otherwise I would have waited a while!!  Thanks for the help.
